3. Research & Development (R&D) Expenditures
Research and development expenses for FY2026 totaled  $14,250 million, compared to $8,675 million in
FY2025. The 64.3% increase was principally driven by employee compensation costs, advanced tape-outs for
the upcoming Rubin GPU platform, and high-bandwidth memory (HBM3e/HBM4) integration research. R&D
expenditure represented approximately 11.5% of total revenue. 
4. Operational Risks & Supply Chain Dynamics
Our  reliance  on  third-party  semiconductor  foundries,  primarily  Taiwan  Semiconductor  Manufacturing
Company (TSMC), represents a concentration of manufacturing risk. Advanced packaging capacity (CoWoS)
remains  the  primary  bottleneck  for  Blackwell  Ultra  B200  shipments.  Additionally,  regulatory  compliance
regarding export controls to specific geographic regions continues to impact potential market capture in Asia-
Pacific markets. 
